no stranger to retirement stipends in Russia — or the scandal that accompanies them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz rails against extremism, AfD sympathizers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:18cdf673e6b8fbc7bf8fbcbffbed3a1a92f2c018778ebd3c5939ac86b6ff3829</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-rails-against-extremism-afd-sympathizers/live-79570924--74b91e3a40aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-rails-against-extremism-afd-sympathizers/live-79570924?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Political extremism threatens Germany's existing social order, Chancellor Merz has said. The Transport Ministry has proposed a five-year plan to improve Germany's ailing railroad infrastructure.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Ex-spy chief sent to pretrial detention on treason charges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce837662138885d8112721372b54acaff7d4b784ab8931a30252e69befc4a846</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T11:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-ex-spy-chief-sent-to-pretrial-detention-on-treason-charges/a-79576300--68ee19fee871.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-ex-spy-chief-sent-to-pretrial-detention-on-treason-charges/a-79576300?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">August Hanning has been remanded into pretrial detention after his arrest. The case has prompted calls for transparency when spies leave the government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's ex-spy chief arrested for espionage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f3899a9fd1a790c970167482212b8cd90010f9db401073fb99f72978880daa1</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T08:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-espionage/a-79560278--e631ff19ef7a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-ex-spy-chief-arrested-for-espionage/a-79560278?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">August Hanning, the man who once led Germany's spy service, is now under investigation for passing on state secrets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Far-right AfD gets first house speaker in a German state parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad6a9ef9c7fbc551b2e0d23f117c5f11437c6bb73b81c79b1bb089aa9b84f466</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T06:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-far-right-afd-gets-first-house-speaker-in-a-german-state-parliament/live-79558497--5fb1cf58f705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-far-right-afd-gets-first-house-speaker-in-a-german-state-parliament/live-79558497?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For the first time since World War II, a far-right party has a house speaker in a German state parliament. And Germany's foreign minister has warned that the climate crisis could fuel extremism.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German politicians warn of antisemitism on October 7 anniversary</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e24befd214d4dafe5a41f42ae04839a4eb5e855ce0c96fb7d80d97e2cef901e3</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-politicians-warn-of-antisemitism-on-october-7-anniversary/a-79583326--969f707c1abe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-politicians-warn-of-antisemitism-on-october-7-anniversary/a-79583326?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leading German politicians including Chancellor Merz and President Steinmeier called for people to reject antisemitism.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Did CDU lawmakers support the far-right AfD?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8392ed477d5c1beb3fd7a66bc9737647a7df732909ca9848b1731c6bebf9ab5c</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T11:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-did-cdu-lawmakers-support-the-far-right-afd/a-79577396--ed4eac4ecf1f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-did-cdu-lawmakers-support-the-far-right-afd/a-79577396?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Lawmakers of the center-right CDU may have voted for the far-right AfD candidate for parliamentary speaker in Saxony-Anhalt. Germany's Social Democrats warn of a "unique breach of taboos."</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Munich up against at least six competitors for 2036 Olympics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96a076eebd0cfebe0b10b40d5c83bb02e0fd519327e91102ba41f608af7fa7aa</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T19:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678--5b4a69f8bd09.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/munich-up-against-at-least-six-competitors-for-2036-olympics/a-79566678?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The International Olympic Committee has revealed the six other countries intending to bid for the 2036 Olympic Games. This comes after Germany selected Munich as its Olympic candidate.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany shaken by espionage and treason allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284015c9b1a86f144f15794ca2eac524de6d2294466427c76ee4bef612ffccfb</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578--c39cf46fd6f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-shaken-by-espionage-and-treason-allegations/a-79566578?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The former head of Germany's foreign intelligence service, the BND, has been accused of spying for a foreign country. Never before has a German official of August Hanning's stature been accused of treason.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc418ead1d33e89c82615450c63b0536f03f141569f9248</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207--cd91ce591124.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/servers-at-munich-s-iconic-oktoberfest-call-for-more-respect/a-79491207?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest is famous the world over for beer, brass band music and Bavarian traditions. But staff are also reporting incidents of racism and sexism, and are taking a stand against discrimination.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41465734b777a0c6b6cf12bfbbc18b0f3bd2fe4b340f6c4eab9c5fbe099e667e</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
